{"uid":"core/llm_key_pool.py","name":"llm_key_pool.py","qualname":"core/llm_key_pool.py","kind":"module","file":"core/llm_key_pool.py","line":1,"end_line":297,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Per-backend LLM API key pool with round-robin rotation and quota cooldown.","description":"sapper-v2 keeps a pool of API keys (``SAPPER_KEY_POOL``) and rotates to the\nnext one when a provider returns an explicit quota/credit error, so a long\nautonomous run survives the exhaustion of any single key. LazyOwn already\nrotates *models/members* on quota (``modules.lazy_loop.task_llm_chain``); this\nmodule adds the orthogonal *key* axis.\n\nThe pool is pure and process-wide. It reads nothing itself: a builder parses\n``payload.json`` once via :func:`build_from_config`, seeding each backend's\npool with its primary key first so a single-key deployment behaves exactly as\nbefore. Keys that hit an explicit quota error are parked for a cooldown window\nand skipped until it elapses; when every key is cooling down the least-recently\nparked one is returned so the caller still makes progress.\n\nConfig shape (``payload.json``):\n    ``llm_key_pool``: either a flat list of extra keys for the default cloud\n    backend (groq), or a mapping ``{backend: [keys, ...]}``. The backend's\n    primary key (``api_key``/``openai_api_key``/...) is always tried first.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["core/llm_key_pool.py::KeyPool","core/llm_key_pool.py::build_from_config","core/llm_key_pool.py::get_key_pool","core/llm_key_pool.py::refresh_from_config","core/llm_key_pool.py::resolve_pooled_key","core/llm_key_pool.py::note_quota_error"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
